<div class="callout callout--tip"><span class="callout__title">Tip</span><strong>Material Recommendation for Indian Climates</strong><p>For coastal cities (Mumbai, Chennai, Kochi, Vizag): Use HDHMR board with PU-sealed edges and veneer or lacquer finish — moisture resistance is non-negotiable. For dry inland cities (Delhi, Jaipur, Hyderabad): Marine plywood with teak veneer is the best all-round choice. For those who want genuine heirloom quality: solid sheesham or teak built by a skilled local carpenter will outlast every family member who uses it.</div>
<p>06</p>
<h2>Finishes &amp; Surface Treatments — The Detail That Makes the Difference</h2>
<p>Two crockery units made from identical materials can look vastly different — and have completely different durability, cleanability, and ageing characteristics — based purely on their surface finish. This is one of the most under-discussed aspects of crockery unit specification.</p>
<p>✨</p>
<h4>High-Gloss Lacquer / PU Finish</h4>
<p>Mirror-smooth reflective surface. Maximum brightness and colour vibrancy. Requires regular wiping to remove fingerprints. Scratches are visible. Best in low-traffic display applications. Polyurethane (PU) is the premium version — more durable and deeper gloss than acrylic lacquer.</p>
<p>PREMIUM</p>
<p>🪨</p>
<h4>Matte / Satin Finish</h4>
<p>No reflective sheen. Fingerprint-resistant. Hides minor scratches. The dominant finish in premium interiors 2023–2026 because it reads as sophisticated rather than showy. Available in virtually any RAL colour. Easier to maintain in daily use than gloss.</p>
<p>🪵</p>
<h4>Natural Wood Veneer</h4>
<p>Real wood surface over engineered substrate. Warmer, more organic appearance than laminate. Requires sealed edges and UV-stable topcoat. Expresses genuine wood character without the cost or weight of solid wood. Protected with PU topcoat for scratch and moisture resistance.</p>
<p>📋</p>
<h4>High-Pressure Laminate (HPL)</h4>
<p>The workhorse finish of Indian furniture. Thousands of patterns including wood, stone, fabric, and solid colours. Extremely scratch, heat, and stain resistant. Edges require aluminium or PVC edge banding to prevent moisture ingress. 1mm thickness is the minimum — 1.2mm or 1.5mm for better edge performance.</p>
<p>🌾</p>
<h4>Duco / Spray Paint Finish</h4>
<p>Industrial spray-applied paint — same as automotive finish. Smooth, even, completely customisable colour. Available in any RAL or NCS colour. More durable than brush-applied paint. Should be topcoated with clear PU for maximum durability. Used extensively in custom-built Indian furniture.</p>
<p>🔮</p>
<h4>Smoked / Bronze Glass Panels</h4>
<p>Tinted glass — smoked grey, bronze, or antique mirror — as door panel inserts. Partially obscures contents while creating a luxurious, jewel-box quality. Hides crockery that doesn't photograph well while displaying premium pieces through selective placement.</p>
