<h2>Complete Buying Checklist — Before You Commission or Purchase</h2>
<p>Use this checklist whether you are commissioning a carpenter-built custom unit or purchasing from a furniture showroom. Every item here corresponds to a common failure point in crockery units across Indian homes.</p>
<h3>Structural &amp; Material Checklist</h3>
<ul>
  <li>✓Confirm board material is BWR plywood, marine plywood, or HDHMR — not particle board or standard MDF, especially in coastal/humid cities</li>
  <li>✓Verify 18mm board thickness for all structural panels (shelves, sides, top, bottom) — 16mm or less is inadequate for crockery weight</li>
  <li>✓Confirm all exposed edges are sealed with 1mm or 1.2mm PVC edge banding — no raw cut edges visible anywhere</li>
  <li>✓Check that back panel is fully laminated or painted on both sides for moisture resistance</li>
  <li>✓Verify shelf load capacity is specified — crockery-loaded shelves should support minimum 20–25kg per shelf</li>
</ul>
<h3>Hardware &amp; Mechanism Checklist</h3>
<ul>
  <li>✓All hinges are soft-close, hydraulic, 165° or 110° opening — specify Hettich, Hafele, Grass, or Blum brand</li>
  <li>✓All drawer slides are full-extension soft-close — not basic ball-bearing slides that stop 80mm from full extension</li>
  <li>✓Glass is confirmed as tempered (toughened) — minimum 4mm for doors up to 600mm wide, 6mm for larger panels</li>
  <li>✓Door magnetic catches or soft-close hinges prevent glass doors from rattling or swinging open unattended</li>
  <li>✓Adjustable shelf pin holes in all display sections — 32mm pitch with steel pins, not plastic</li>
</ul>
<h3>Lighting &amp; Interior Checklist</h3>
<ul>
  <li>✓Interior LED lighting specified — confirm 2700K colour temperature, not 4000K or 6500K</li>
  <li>✓Lighting is on a separate switch or motion-sensor circuit — not wired to the main room light</li>
  <li>✓Non-slip shelf liner included or specified for glassware sections</li>
  <li>✓Ventilation gap or perforations in back panel for air circulation in closed sections</li>
  <li>✓Electrical wiring for interior lights is concealed within the cabinet — not surface-run with exposed conduit</li>
</ul>
<h3>Sizing &amp; Fit Checklist</h3>
<ul>
  <li>✓Unit depth is minimum 380mm — confirmed against your largest dinner plate diameter plus 30mm clearance</li>
  <li>✓At least one shelf height is 300mm+ for tall glassware and champagne flutes</li>
  <li>✓Unit will be wall-anchored at top — confirm anchor method and wall type compatibility</li>
  <li>✓Cornice and plinth pieces included for finished appearance at ceiling and floor junction</li>
  <li>✓Countertop height at 850–900mm if unit includes a serving surface</li>
</ul>
